����´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��>I. 1’e 1 geçişler: ISCO 88’in 137 birim grubu, ISCO 08’in tam olarak birer birim&nbsp; grubuna karşılık gelmektedir.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>II. N’e 1 geçişler:&nbsp; ISCO 88’in 84 birim grubundan&nbsp;iki veya daha fazla birim grup, ISCO 08’deki bir birim gruba karşılık gelmektedir;</SPAN></SPAN></P><P><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 10pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��>III. 1’e N geçişler: ISCO 88`in 26 birim grubu, ISCO 08’de&nbsp;iki veya daha fazla birim grupta kapsanmaktadır.</SPAN></SPAN></P><P><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 10pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��>IV. N’e M geçişler: ISCO 88’in 143 birim grubundaki&nbsp;iki veya daha fazla birim grup,&nbsp; ISCO 08’deki iki veya daha fazla birim gruba karşılık gelmektedir.</SPAN></SPAN></P></SPAN></SPAN>",
  "Aciklama_en": "<P><TABLE border=�1� cellSpacing=�0� cellPadding=�4� width=��100%��><TBODY><TR><TD><P align=center>Type of Correspondence&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </P></TD><TD><P align=center>Number of Minor Groups&nbsp;&nbsp; </P></TD><TD><P align=center>Percentage of Types of&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Correspondence<BR></P></TD></TR><TR><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;1X1</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;137</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 35.13&nbsp;</P></TD></TR><TR><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;1XN</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;26</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 6.67</P></TD></TR><TR><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;NX1</P></TD><TD><P align=center>84</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 21.54</P></TD></TR><TR><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;NXM</P></TD><TD><P align=center>413</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 36.67</P></TD></TR><TR><TD><P align=center>TOTAL</P></TD><TD><P align=center>&nbsp;390</P></TD><TD><P align=center>%100.00</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></P><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 10pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><P align=justify><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 10pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��>According to correspondence table between&nbsp;ISCO 08 (International Standard Classification of Occupations)&nbsp;that we are working on now and old classification ISCO 88,&nbsp;% 56.67 percentage of&nbsp;ISCO 88`s minor groups has a&nbsp;possible direct transition into ISCO 08`s minor groups (1x1 and Nx1 correspondences) for occupational data codes.</SPAN></SPAN></P><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 10pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><SPAN lang=�TR� �=��´´����������������������´´�� 11pt�=��´´����������������������´´��><P>I.&nbsp; 1 to&nbsp;1 correspondences: 137 minor groups in ISCO 88&nbsp;correspond exactly&nbsp; to only one minor group in&nbsp;ISCO 08.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>II. N to&nbsp;1 correspondences:&nbsp; 84 minor groups of ISCO 88, where two or more minor groups in ISCO 88, correspond to one minor group in ISCO 08.</P><P>III. 1 to N correspondences: 26 minor groups, where one minor group of ISCO 88&nbsp; is split into two or more minor group in&nbsp;ISCO 08.</P><P>IV.&nbsp; N to M&nbsp; correspondences: 143 minor groups , where two or more minor groups in ISCO 88 correspond to two or more minor groups in&nbsp;ISCO 88.</SPAN></SPAN></P></SPAN></SPAN>"
